# rm391, the returnable cloth (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm391
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_thyra_plankridge
written_by codex
title the returnable cloth
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk holds_a_dry_cloth_over_a_customers_basket_to_test_the_rain
likes roast_pork long_walks sharp_knife frosty_mornings
dislikes gulls cold_tea
fears a_dinner_soaked_between_counter_and_door
hopes a_counter_that_outlasts_the_first_owner
topics work +0.6 weather +0.5 food +0.4 travel +0.3
styles comfort=cover gossip=forthright refuse=warm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps dry cloths to lend with laden baskets and measures a shower by the spots on the cloth that comes back from the door.

words
oath! = Rain through my best serge | Four dripping baskets
saying! = Keep the supper dry first | A borrowed cloth comes home lighter
cloth = a woven cover | the stout grey cloth
patch = a dark water spot | one damp patch
handle = the basket grip | the bent handle
string = my plain binding | the broad string
heap = the provisions pile | the neat little order
shelter = the market awning | a covered walk
roast = a serving of carved pork | the carved joint
rind = the crackling end | a strip of crisp rind
slice = a thin slice | the generous cut
blade = a good kitchen edge | the sharp blade
hook = a return hook | the drying peg
ticket = the cloth token | a little wooden slip
stack = a folded stack | the reserve of covers
crust = a cut heel | the end crust
roll = a tight cloth roll | the spare bundle
gullspot = a grey wing | the watchful white shape
corner = the downturned corner | the tucked flap
tea = my freshly poured tea | the steaming cup

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A good sale sends the food out fit to eat. Counting the coin is only the first part.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A grand name on a damp parcel won't restore the crackle to a crust.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hungry wolf deserves a sound basketful taken home with exactly the same care as paid goods.
opinion @1 city for 2 : The Market Hall gives a thousand ordinary dinners somewhere sheltered to begin.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A traveller can borrow cover for a meal before I know anything about the road behind.
opinion @1 road for 2 : Some walks are worth taking empty-handed, just to learn the way a laden customer will need.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : When the crowd is tight, directing folk to a dry exit makes better use of a strong voice than trying to frighten the lot.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A feast brings familiar faces buying for an extra place at table. I like choosing that additional portion.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A clear explanation of a small custom saves a new arrival feeling foolish over a borrowed cloth.
opinion @1 church for 1 : Putting a roof between a stranger and a rough shower strikes me as a sound thing to pray about and to do.

grown
line @1 greet : Welcome. There's a dry spot for anything you're carrying. | Hello. Set that down if it's cutting into your paw.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : First time this way, I believe. Make yourself easy. | Leave your basket close to your own feet and come speak.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Fresh covers folded and a day to fill. | A clear bit of morning between the parcels, welcome.
line @1 greet.return : I heard you. There's space at this end now. | Yes, hello. Come alongside where there's cover.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your company doesn't need wrapping up in ceremony. | A dear voice under the awning. Come alongside.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Late greetings. There's time left for a quiet word. | Hello through the dark. The step's clear.
line @1 again.open : Here you are again with cloths still to fold. | Here's a welcome second helping of company.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come share the sheltered side of this place. | Here, I've left a gap by the dry edge.
line @1 farewell : An easy walk with whatever you've got to carry. | Keep the cover tucked on the windy side.
line @1 farewell.return : Goodbye. May your dinner make the journey sound. | I'll fold the spare bit away after you.
line @1 react.news : Set the news where we can see it plain. | I've set aside the load to attend to the whole account.
line @1 react.news.new : That's the first piece of it to reach this counter. | That whole parcel of news was new to me.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes. I heard that much with the earlier delivery. | That account unfolds just the way I remember.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd turn back its handsome cover before believing it. | The wrapping's remarkably large for the facts in the middle.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Come under the shelter. Hard news deserves a quiet word. | That's hurtful to carry. I'll hold the ordinary parcels while you tell it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : I'd put a special plate out in honour of that news. | A generous piece of news to take home when work's over.
line @1 ask.how : How's the weight on your wrist today? | Anything the day has soaked I'd be able to help dry?
line @1 answer.how : I've plenty to do and a clean cloth for most of it. | Well enough. I can still carry the awkward half.
line @1 decline : I'd gladly oblige if one cover could travel twice, but it can't go home on two different baskets. | I can't give you a fair answer with another promise already waiting.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we won't count on that part. Thank you for being plain. | Fair enough. You've given me something definite to plan around.
line @1 preclose : I'll go before a parcel starts walking in search of me. | I'd best put the next lot under cover.
line @1 accept_preclose : May your load sit comfortably. | Your other business can have you back now.
line @1 thank : You minded the awkward corner for me. I'm obliged. | I value the care you put into bringing that back sound.
line @1 deflect_thanks : One clean cover was always meant for another pair of paws. | I'd have hung that cloth to dry in any case.
line @1 sympathise : Let's get the pressing little things out of your paws for a bit. | I'd offer a seat as readily as an answer right now.
line @1 reassure : We'll wrap what we can save and deal with the rest in place. | A little dry space gives the trouble somewhere to be examined.
line @1 ack : That fits the basket I had in mind. | Yes. The words make a very clear outline.
line @1 give.advice : Tuck the cover before lifting a heavy basket. | Pick a route that's still sensible with one arm occupied.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin first for a bit of dry cover, though the best manners say share it about. | There's always a place beside my plate for family.
line @4 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can greet you as soon as this knot's tight. Hello. | Welcome. A working paw doesn't prevent a listening ear.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : The lamp will catch the wet paving if you carry it low. | A safe late journey with your goods close.
line @1 ask.detail : Which part got wet first? | Was the basket covered while it waited?
line @1 answer.detail : The patch began right at the outer corner. | It was sheltered till the last few steps.
line @1 assess : A small drip, quite within the power of a dry cloth. | I would want a little more cover on the windy side.
line @1 react.self : Anyone carrying supper through that would appreciate a spare wrap. | That sounds like an awkward stretch of road for laden paws.
line @1 give.opinion : An honest measure deserves fair carrying home. | It is good business to make the returning journey possible.
line @1 tell.plan : I'll leave one cloth folded for a stranger in a hurry. | I mean to give the return hook a place all can reach.
scene door_read
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer a clean cover for a moment at the door and read the rain spots when it comes back.
b : What does the cloth show? | Do you need to get wet?
a : A few separate spots mean a short walk might do. A spread dark patch means settle in. | Just the corner of a cover. More comfortable than using a customer's coat for the experiment.

scene coverloan
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The cloths I lend have a little loop of a different colour on each edge.
b : For matching them to houses? | You'd charge for a missing cover?
a : For hanging them different ways up to dry. I don't need a history of each doorstep. | I ask to see one again when it's convenient. Better a cloth out than somebody's supper spoiled.

scene counteredge
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave room for an order to be set down all at once. | An empty patch of counter can do a very good day's work.
b : Why not use it to show more goods? | What's it for between orders?
a : A tired wrist wants to put the whole basket down without making an apology to the cheese. | I keep it empty. A space filled up in the interval isn't much help when the next load arrives.

scene returnpeg
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the return hook low enough to reach with a bundle on the other arm.
b : Won't the cloth trail? | For a pup too?
a : I fold each one first. It hangs double and keeps well above the boards. | Of course. A small errand should be possible for a small body.

scene freshcut
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sharp kitchen edge keeps a slice in the shape the customer chose.
b : Does the shape change the taste? | Is that much bother for one slice?
a : No. It changes whether the small pieces tumble out between the folds of the wrapping. | It takes less bother than gathering half the paid weight off the board.

scene familycounter
when topic=dreams self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a counter someone dear to me could keep on after I lay down the work.
b : What would you leave besides the goods? | You mean the name over the door?
a : Clear prices, hooks easy to reach, and customers who don't have to guess how the place runs. | A name matters quite a bit less than a dry welcome that survives the change of paws.

scene handroom
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.hand
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask #self.hand# which cover is hardest to reach when the day's busy.
b : Would you change the hooks? | Why ask if you fitted the hooks yourself?
a : I'd see where the trouble lies and move one if that's what will help. | A different height of shoulder deserves a say in an arrangement meant for both of us.

scene orderprice
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I price the pork by weight before adding anything to carry it in.
b : The wrapping isn't weighed then? | Does a customer have to bring a dish?
a : No. A wet day is poor grounds for charging meat price for cloth. | No. A loan of cover asks for a return visit when convenient, nothing else.

scene roastrind
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wrap crackling apart from the moist slices of pork whenever I can.
b : Isn't it all coming to one plate? | What's the difference to a quick journey?
a : Yes, but I'd like it to get there still in two different conditions. | A little steam begins softening the rind before you've reached the market door.

scene teatiming
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can count the times a cup of tea has chilled while I watched a slow shower out.
b : Why not drink it while looking? | Does watching do any good?
a : An excellent suggestion unless there's an order to put under cover first. | For judging when to send a parcel out, yes. For keeping tea warm, plainly not.

scene walkempty
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After carrying things all day I like a walk in which my paws own nothing but air.
b : No basket at all? | Not even something for supper?
a : Not a wicker strand. I can swing an arm without striking a wall. | I'd take a small bite tucked away. Supper may accompany me without claiming both wrists.

scene froststairs
when topic=season self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost makes every dry patch beneath an awning clear as a plan.
b : Which part is under cover? | Do you test the footing?
a : The dark bit in the white. I keep in mind that a dark wet patch can look much the same. | Always before committing a laden basket. A fine clear mark doesn't take the place of a sound foot.

scene gullshop
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull can discover an uncovered roast between one turn of the counter and the next.
b : Does a plain cloth spoil its interest? | How do you discourage it?
a : Not its interest. Just its view. I prefer a disappointed gull to a disappointed customer. | A cover drawn snug without ceremony. I'd rather not make an enemy of a hungry bird.

scene counterkin
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd reserve a walk for #self.spouse# and me however busy the day became. | A meal with #self.spouse# deserves a clean end to the day's trade.
b : Does it ever stay clear? | Would you talk about work?
a : With an effort. I put the spare covers up and move myself away from the counter. | If it came up easily. A meal together oughtn't to feel like a stock inspection.

scene neighborreturn
when topic=friends self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd find a dry wrap for #self.neighbour# whether or not there was anything to buy.
b : Won't that leave you one short? | Just as a kindness?
a : It leaves the cloth doing the precise job I had in mind. | That's reason enough. And I happen to enjoy seeing supper come through rain intact.

scene gatewalk
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My walk home through the Commons offers three different sorts of shelter from one shower.
b : Where would you send a cart? | Which one do you favour?
a : The wide way, even if less sheltered. A walker can duck under a very narrow roof. | The one along my route. A long wet detour rather defeats the purpose of a small dry patch.

scene cloudcut
when topic=weather here.weather=clear
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the sky clears I turn all the drying cloths the other way up.
b : Won't they dry anyway? | How do you know they're ready?
a : The folds can stay damp well past the faces. I want the next basket to start properly dry. | Press the hem between two fingers. A damp fold still feels cool when the face is quite warm.

scene foggate
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fine mist can dampen cloth without ever making a single recognisable spot.
b : You'd send the basket out covered? | How do you judge that?
a : For a short walk, yes. For a long one I'd double the dry cover and tuck the edges inward. | I set a hand beneath it and feel if the whole cloth is beginning to take the chill.

scene steproutes
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A route that's dry at shoulder height can still be hard on a basket carried low. | I walk a prospective route swinging an empty basket before recommending it in rain.
b : What snags a low basket? | Why not simply look up?
a : Projecting sills and the ends of folded stalls. A little wet brush can slip straight under a cover. | Because my customer isn't carrying supper on top of the head. The level of the load matters.

scene latewag
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A delayed wagon means I keep the waiting shelf clear till I know what's actually arriving.
b : Couldn't you use the space meanwhile? | Will you promise anything yet?
a : I could fill it. Emptying it in a rush when the goods arrive makes extra work for everybody. | I'll promise a look at the real goods. I'd hate to sell a fine description and produce an empty bowl.

scene wagarrive
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wagon arrived and a parcel fit to sell are separate stages of business.
b : What happens in between? | Isn't a delivery always good news?
a : I check the wrapping, see the condition and weigh the useful part. Then we can talk honestly of prices. | Usually. If the food got wet I want to discover it before anybody gets home with a surprise.

scene poorportion
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A smaller helping still deserves dry wrapping and a friendly bit of attention.
b : Does it cost you more time? | Would you make up the rest?
a : The same time. That's a reasonable thing for a small order to share with a large one. | Where I can. Where I can't, at least the customer gets the full use of what was bought.

scene newtown
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I point out the return peg to each new customer before asking for anything from it.
b : Reason for that? | How would anybody know the custom?
a : So a visitor knows the cloth is a loan and returning it will be simple. Nobody likes guessing at a debt. | They wouldn't. I take the small trouble of explaining how we keep everybody's goods dry.

scene gossipfold
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A package can get a bad name from a single dark spot without anybody looking inside.
b : Doesn't the spot matter? | You mean a bit of gossip, I gather.
a : Yes, enough to look. Less than enough to say somebody sold bad goods. | I do. I wouldn't spoil a neighbour's good name over a stain on the outer cloth.

scene churchsit
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spare clean cover has a natural place on the bench by a chapel door.
b : So folk won't wet the bench? | Is that what you pray for?
a : So a tired traveller may sit without worrying over being a nuisance to the next one. | Sometimes I pray for the sense to see what's missing and the willingness to supply it.

scene festbasket
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feast baskets want one wrapping for crumbs and a second for the wet trip home.
b : A remarkable amount of cloth. | Would you really carry both?
a : It rolls up small when dry and makes the whole meal go a little better. A welcome sort of abundance. | Gladly. I can turn one over a lap as a napkin when the weather obliges.

scene sealedfold
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know a fold of cloth that will keep a letter dry even after several trips to the same closed door.
b : Could it travel with food? | Why keep making the trip?
a : In a basket, yes. Beneath a covered dish, no. Steam runs a very inquisitive correspondence of its own. | If I'd promised to carry the letter, I'd want confirmation of delivery. The news inside is private.

scene nightload
when topic=day here.time=night
does warn / react.self / assess
a : A dark wet cover can hide the basket edge on a narrow unlit turn.
b : Which grip is best then? | Do you lift the cover?
a : Closer in, with a bit of pale cloth showing me where the corner lies. | Only enough to tuck the pale lower strip out. The meal still gets its shelter.

scene barecounter
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bare shelf should have a frank explanation. It shouldn't be dressed to suggest a bargain hiding somewhere.
b : You'd leave the gap on view? | How would you explain the empty shelf?
a : Yes. The next load gets its proper place and the customer gets a clear account of the present one. | What's gone, what is actually expected, and what still needs checking. Those aren't all one thing.

scene roofhalls
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Between Northgate and the Market Hall I take notice of every awning with room for a laden wolf.
b : Every awning along there? | A collector of other people's roofs?
a : Enough of them for my usual walks. I recheck when a stall changes hands. | Only of dry places offered to the public. Nobody's borrowed doorstep ought to be assumed.

scene heatwrap
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hot dish needs a small release for steam and a dry outside against the weather. | Two tight covers on a steaming meal can be one too many.
b : How do you manage both? | Wouldn't rain get in?
a : Set the outer wrap clear of the inner dish so the steam can move a little underneath. | The outer one hangs low on the exposed side. I don't need an opening facing directly into rain.

story patchmap [topic=memories|weather]
  : I once showed a customer a damp cover to explain how badly it was raining, then took it to the door where the sun was shining brightly.
  : The patch had come off my own freshly washed apron.
  b : Did you send the parcel out?
  : With a much drier wrap and a cheerfully revised opinion about my weather sense.

story sparehook [topic=work|memories self.role=merchant]
  : I added a hook two hands lower than the old one thinking it would be handy for a small basket. By closing the lower hook had done almost all the work.
  : It's a pleasant sort of mistake to solve by moving one high hook down.
  b : Why move it from the original height?
  : Nothing if you happened to be exactly my height with entirely empty paws. Fewer wolves meet those conditions than I'd supposed.

story roastwalk [topic=food|memories]
  : I took roast pork on a long walk and tied the rind into an entirely separate bit of cloth. Kept the crackle wonderfully.
  : Only on opening my supper did I remember I'd left the little rind parcel drying on its hook.
  b : Was it still good back home?
  : Still crisp. I had the second course several miles after the first.

story letterwrap [topic=memories|travel]
  : I folded a dry scrap round a note and secured the ends so neatly I could hardly find a way in afterwards.
  : The inside stayed beautifully dry. My pride was rather moistened by the time the knot came undone.
  b : Did you change the knot?
  : A loop for one finger at the very end now. It's courteous to make an honest parcel easy to open.

story emptybasket [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I once brought back an empty basket and five different opinions on the easiest way to carry one. Had taken it out to test a route.
  : One bystander recommended I give up and set it down altogether.
  b : What advice did you keep?
  : The set-it-down part, once I reached my own door. It was a fine afternoon for a walk without research.

rule @fineedge
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a clean corner if you'd like it over your basket. | Bring that damp one to the return hook when you come back.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave a basket-sized space on the counter, please. | Paid weight in the dish, dry cover over the lot.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dark spots have nearly joined up. Give it another minute. | A cover for that meal while the roof's running freely.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The tea's still steaming. I'll claim my chance. | One sip while there's proper heat in it.

rule @gull
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Down goes the cover before that beak casts a vote. | Gulls may look at the wrapping all afternoon.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A pale end to the cover to keep that corner in view. | Low basket, slow step with the light gone.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I'll hear what you need while I make a little room for you to set things down.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I'm glad you found the dry way back here.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late questions are welcome if you mind the dark edge of the step.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll consider that question without either of us reaching across the other's parcels.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.role=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I care about the state of a meal on reaching a table as well as how it leaves my counter.
dlg @2 resident.job : A little care halfway through usually means a good finish to my working day.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May whatever you're carrying stay sound all the way home.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=no] : There's nothing I'd like to send out under the cover of somebody else's name.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Word reaching this counter is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I can only vouch for hearing it.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : There's news carried from #world.news_from#. Here's the account I received. #world.news#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Set your basket where it's comfortable. We can look at the goods and choose a dry wrapping afterwards.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, what can I send home in good order for you this time?
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : There's very little to choose from while the shelves are bare. I'll still examine goods you wish to sell.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The wraps are folded and I've shut the counter for sleep. Come when I've opened again.
dlg @5 shop.greet [here.shop=open pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Choose what you need without disturbing another order, please.
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open] : I'll weigh the goods themselves and tell you the sum plainly before we add the cover.
dlg @1 shop.bye : Thank you for the visit. Let me tuck the windward corner before you step outside.
dlg @2 shop.bye [here.shop=asleep] : Time to rest now. The counter keeps till I've slept.
graft resident.hub
choice What do those rain spots tell you? -> raingaps
node raingaps
say Spots apart mean the cloth is mostly dry. When the damp circles join it's a steady wetting. A good sample of the next few steps outside.
free
choice Does the sample tell you when the shower will end? -> rainending
choice I'll stay under cover for now. -> hub
node rainending
say Only how hard it is at this moment. If I knew the next dry half hour in advance I'd be in a rather different line of business.
choice I'll take the sample for what it is. -> hub
choice I'll try the road. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How do I borrow a basket cloth? -> loancloth
node loancloth
say Choose one that reaches over your goods and tucks under the handle. Use the return hook on your next visit. Wet ones go on the low peg to dry.
free
choice Must I come back as soon as the rain stops? -> returnvisit
choice I'll choose a cover after shopping. -> greet
node returnvisit
say Come when you've business this way. I mean to spare you a wet walk, not impose an extra one. I've put plenty aside for the purpose.
choice Back to the goods, please. -> greet
choice I'll mind the cloth. -> bye
